# What `railway up` leaves out of the upload (gitignore syntax; .gitignore applies too). The Railway service runs
# only the API (`python server.py`, RUN_WORKER=0): Python code, requirements.txt, the seeded_*.json files api.py
# serves and agent_id_stats.json. The frontend is on Vercel (the hosted API only redirects to it), the worker is on
# the GCP VM. Anything uploaded is a file that could be exposed by a future mistake, so upload nothing extra.
# `python3 -m pytest` is not run on Railway; CI runs it before this deploys.
#
# Kept on purpose: package.json / package-lock.json (they decide how Nixpacks detects the build; not worth touching).

